WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.630
Cut your finger, and within
minutes the bleeding stops.

2
00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:08.260
Yet that same blood flows freely
through every other vessel in your body.

3
00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:11.580
Clotting also protects
you: it keeps blood in,

4
00:00:11.630 --> 00:00:13.290
and pathogens out.

5
00:00:13.340 --> 00:00:16.010
So how does blood flow freely everywhere,

6
00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:18.370
yet seal a cut within minutes?

7
00:00:18.420 --> 00:00:21.710
In this mission, you'll watch
the first responders arrive:

8
00:00:21.760 --> 00:00:25.000
platelets, sticking at
the cut to form a plug.

9
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:30.120
Then you'll see how a chain of enzyme
reactions turns a small injury into a fast,

10
00:00:30.170 --> 00:00:31.700
large response.

11
00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:36.080
Your mission: explain how blood can
flow freely through every vessel,

12
00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:38.110
yet seal a cut within minutes.
